<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Deliberately empty.

    Notarisation requires the Hardened Runtime, and the Hardened Runtime's
    restrictions are all things this app does not do: no JIT, no unsigned
    executable memory, no DYLD environment overrides, and no loading of
    third-party libraries into its own process.

    It does spawn `node` as a child process, but library validation governs code
    loaded INTO this process, not separate processes — so that needs no
    entitlement either. Adding one "just in case" would weaken the runtime for
    no reason and has to be justified to notarisation.

    The app is intentionally NOT App Sandboxed: it reads Claude's transcripts and
    credentials from arbitrary user-chosen paths, which is the whole job.
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
